Relevant columns and their possible usage  
• FORUMS."Title": locate the parent forum titled “General” and fetch its id.  
• FORUMS."Id": join to FORUMTOPICS to know which topics live in a given forum; also to find child‑forums whose "ParentForumId" equals the id of “General”.  
• FORUMS."ParentForumId": detects sub‑forums (children of “General”).  
• FORUMTOPICS."ForumId": tells in which (sub‑)forum every topic resides.  
• FORUMTOPICS."Id": primary key used to join to FORUMMESSAGES.  
• FORUMTOPICS."Title": topic title to be returned.  
• FORUMTOPICS."CreationDate": topic creation date to be returned.  
• FORUMTOPICS."TotalViews": already‑stored topic view counter to be returned.  
• FORUMMESSAGES."ForumTopicId": matches a topic; used for counting replies.  
• FORUMMESSAGES."PostUserId": distinct user ids that replied.  
• FORUMMESSAGES."Id": join‑key to FORUMMESSAGEVOTES.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."ForumMessageId": votes attached to a message → used to sum up up‑votes.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."Id": each record is an up‑vote, so counting rows gives number of up‑votes.  

Typical conditions  
• WHERE FORUMS."Title" ILIKE '%general%'                -- find “General” parent forum (case‑insensitive)  
• WHERE FORUMS."ParentForumId" = <General_Id>           -- pick its children (sub‑forums)  
• WHERE FORUMTOPICS."ForumId" IN ( …sub‑forum ids… )    -- restrict topics to those sub‑forums  
• ORDER BY FORUMTOPICS."CreationDate" ASC              -- earliest topics first  
• LIMIT 5                                               -- earliest five  

Below are ten step‑by‑step Snowflake queries (each different, capped to 20 rows) that explore the task’s data all the way up to a final aggregated query; adjust database / schema / table names exactly as shown.

