Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their possible usage  
• FORUMS."Title": locate the parent forum titled “General” and fetch its id.  
• FORUMS."Id": join to FORUMTOPICS to know which topics live in a given forum; also to find child‑forums whose "ParentForumId" equals the id of “General”.  
• FORUMS."ParentForumId": detects sub‑forums (children of “General”).  
• FORUMTOPICS."ForumId": tells in which (sub‑)forum every topic resides.  
• FORUMTOPICS."Id": primary key used to join to FORUMMESSAGES.  
• FORUMTOPICS."Title": topic title to be returned.  
• FORUMTOPICS."CreationDate": topic creation date to be returned.  
• FORUMTOPICS."TotalViews": already‑stored topic view counter to be returned.  
• FORUMMESSAGES."ForumTopicId": matches a topic; used for counting replies.  
• FORUMMESSAGES."PostUserId": distinct user ids that replied.  
• FORUMMESSAGES."Id": join‑key to FORUMMESSAGEVOTES.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."ForumMessageId": votes attached to a message → used to sum up up‑votes.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."Id": each record is an up‑vote, so counting rows gives number of up‑votes.  

Typical conditions  
• WHERE FORUMS."Title" ILIKE '%general%'                -- find “General” parent forum (case‑insensitive)  
• WHERE FORUMS."ParentForumId" = <General_Id>           -- pick its children (sub‑forums)  
• WHERE FORUMTOPICS."ForumId" IN ( …sub‑forum ids… )    -- restrict topics to those sub‑forums  
• ORDER BY FORUMTOPICS."CreationDate" ASC              -- earliest topics first  
• LIMIT 5                                               -- earliest five  

Below are ten step‑by‑step Snowflake queries (each different, capped to 20 rows) that explore the task’s data all the way up to a final aggregated query; adjust database / schema / table names exactly as shown.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Find the forum record whose title contains the word "General".
SELECT
    "Id",
    "Title"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMS"
WHERE "Title" ILIKE '%general%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: List the first 20 sub‑forums whose parent is the “General” forum (using the id found in query 1).
SELECT
    "Id"      AS "SubForumId",
    "Title"   AS "SubForumTitle",
    "ParentForumId"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMS"
WHERE "ParentForumId" = <REPLACE_WITH_GENERAL_ID>
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Peek at topics located in any of the sub‑forums under “General”.
SELECT
    "Id"            AS "TopicId",
    "ForumId",
    "Title",
    "CreationDate",
    "TotalViews"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS"
WHERE "ForumId" IN ( <REPLACE_WITH_SUBFORUM_IDS_COMMA_SEPARATED> )
ORDER BY "CreationDate"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Retrieve messages that belong to one sample topic (replace with a real topic id from query 3).
SELECT
    "Id"            AS "MessageId",
    "ForumTopicId",
    "PostUserId",
    "PostDate"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES"
WHERE "ForumTopicId" = <TOPIC_ID>
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Count how many messages (replies) each of the first 20 topics has.
SELECT
    fm."ForumTopicId"              AS "TopicId",
    COUNT(*)                       AS "ReplyCount"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES" fm
WHERE fm."ForumTopicId" IN ( <REPLACE_WITH_TOPIC_IDS_COMMA_SEPARATED> )
GROUP BY fm."ForumTopicId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Count distinct users who replied in the same set of topics.
SELECT
    fm."ForumTopicId"              AS "TopicId",
    COUNT(DISTINCT fm."PostUserId") AS "DistinctUserReplies"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES" fm
WHERE fm."ForumTopicId" IN ( <REPLACE_WITH_TOPIC_IDS_COMMA_SEPARATED> )
GROUP BY fm."ForumTopicId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Count up‑votes for all messages inside the chosen topics.
SELECT
    m."ForumTopicId"               AS "TopicId",
    COUNT(v."Id")                  AS "TotalUpVotes"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES" m
LEFT JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
       ON v."ForumMessageId" = m."Id"
WHERE m."ForumTopicId" IN ( <REPLACE_WITH_TOPIC_IDS_COMMA_SEPARATED> )
GROUP BY m."ForumTopicId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Bring together replies, distinct users and up‑votes for every topic under sub‑forums of “General”.
SELECT
    t."Id"                                      AS "TopicId",
    COUNT(m."Id")                               AS "ReplyCount",
    COUNT(DISTINCT m."PostUserId")              AS "DistinctUsers",
    COUNT(v."Id")                               AS "TotalUpVotes"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS" t
LEFT JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES" m
       ON m."ForumTopicId" = t."Id"
LEFT JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
       ON v."ForumMessageId" = m."Id"
WHERE t."ForumId" IN (
    SELECT "Id"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMS"
    WHERE "ParentForumId" = <REPLACE_WITH_GENERAL_ID>
)
GROUP BY t."Id"
ORDER BY t."CreationDate"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Fetch the earliest five topics in those sub‑forums (no aggregates, just to identify them).
SELECT
    t."Id"          AS "TopicId",
    t."Title",
    t."CreationDate",
    t."TotalViews"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS" t
WHERE t."ForumId" IN (
    SELECT "Id"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMS"
    WHERE "ParentForumId" = <REPLACE_WITH_GENERAL_ID>
)
ORDER BY t."CreationDate" ASC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Final composite query – return creation date, topic title, parent forum title, reply count, 
--                  distinct user replies, total up‑votes and total views for the earliest five topics.
SELECT
    t."CreationDate"                                           AS "CreationDate",
    t."Title"                                                  AS "TopicTitle",
    pf."Title"                                                 AS "ParentForumTitle",
    COALESCE(COUNT(m."Id"), 0)                                 AS "ReplyCount",
    COALESCE(COUNT(DISTINCT m."PostUserId"), 0)                AS "DistinctUserReplies",
    COALESCE(COUNT(v."Id"), 0)                                 AS "TotalUpVotes",
    COALESCE(t."TotalViews", 0)                                AS "TotalViews"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS" t
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMS" sf
     ON sf."Id" = t."ForumId"                                  -- sub‑forum
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMS" pf
     ON pf."Id" = sf."ParentForumId"                           -- parent forum (“General”)
LEFT JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES" m
     ON m."ForumTopicId" = t."Id"
LEFT JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
     ON v."ForumMessageId" = m."Id"
WHERE pf."Title" ILIKE '%general%'
GROUP BY
    t."Id",            -- keep topic grain
    t."CreationDate",
    t."Title",
    pf."Title",
    t."TotalViews"
ORDER BY t."CreationDate" ASC
LIMIT 5;
```

